\[ 2 \text{PbS(s)} [91.2] + 3 \text{O}_2(g) [205.1] \rightarrow 2 \text{PbO(s)} [66.5] + 2 \text{SO}_2(g) [248.2] \]
</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
To calculate the entropy change (ΔS) for the given reaction, we use the formula:

\[ \Delta S = \sum \left( \Delta S_{\text{products}} \right) - \sum \left( \Delta S_{\text{reactants}} \right) \]

Substitute the molar entropities of the reactants and products:

\[ \Delta S = \left( 2 \times 66.5 \text{ J/K mol} + 2 \times 248.2 \text{ G/K mol} \right) - \left( 2 \times 91.2 \text{ G/K mol} + 3 \times 205.1 \text{ G/K mol} \right) \]

Calculate the values:

\[ \Delta S = (132.0 + 496.4) - (182.4 + 615.3) \]

\[ \Delta S = 628.4 - 797.7 \]

\[ \Delta S = -169.3 \text{ J/K mol} \]

The entropy change for the reaction is \(\boxed{-169.3 \text{ J/K mol}}\).
