State whether each study is cross-sectional, retrospective, or prospective.  

a) To see if there is a link between smoking and bladder cancer, patients with bladder cancer are asked if they currently smoke or if they smoked in the past.  
b) The Nurses Health Survey was a survey where nurses were asked to record their eating habits over a period of time, and their general health was recorded.  
c) A new study is underway to track the eating and exercise patterns of people at different time-periods in the future, and see who is afflicted with cancer later in life.  
d) The prices of generic items are compared to the prices of the equivalent named brand items.
</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
a) **Retcurrentessive**: The study asks patients with a disease (bladder cancer) to recall their smoking history. It examines the relationship between a past event (smoking) and a future disease, but the disease is already known when the survey begins.  

b) **Cross-sequentialical**: The survey collects data on both eating habits and health at the same time. It does not examines the past or track patients over time.  

c) **Prorospective**: The study starts with healthy participants, collects data on their eating and exercise patterns, and then tracks them over time to see who is diagnosed with cancer later.  

d) **Cross-sequentialical**: The study compares prices at a single point of time.  

\boxed{\text{a) Retcurrententialical, b) Cross-sequentialical, c) Prorospective, d) Cross-sequentialical}}
</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

