Distance A travels in these 3 hours = Speed × Time
Distance A travels = 10 kmph × 3 hours = 30 km

Now, when B starts cycling, A is 30 km away from the start.

Now, we need to find out how long it will take B to catch up to A.

A's speed = 10 kmph
B's speed = 20 kmph

Relative speed of B with A = B's speed - A's speed
Relative speed = 20 kmph - 10 kmph = 10 kmph

Time it takes for B to catch up to A = Distance A is away from the start / Relative speed
Time it takes for B to catch up to A = 30 km / 10 kmph = 3 hours

Now, we can find the distance from the start when B catches up to A.

