   - By the definition of Fréchet differentiability, there exists a constant $c \geq 1$ such that for all $y \in \mathcal{U}$,
     \[
     \frac{f(y) - f(x^*)}{\|y - x^*\|} \leq c \langle \nabla f(x^*) (y - x^*) \rangle.
     \]
   - By the quasiim principle,
     \[
     \liminf_{y \to x^*, y \in \mathcal{U}} \frac{f(y) - f(x^*)}{\|y - x^*\|} \geq 0.
     \]
   - Combining these, for any $y \in \mathcal{U}$,
     \[
     \frac{f(y) - f(x^*)}{\|y - x^*\|} \leq c \langle \nabla f(x^*) (y - x^*) \rangle.
     \]
