\[
A_{vf}' = A_v \times \frac{1}{2^6} = 100 \times \frac{1}{64} = 1.5625 \text{ V}
\]

The transfer-loop gain is now:
\[
A_{tf}' = A_{vf}' \times m_v = 1.5625 \times 0.1 = 0.15625 \text{ V}
\]

The closed-loop voltage gain with the altered \( A_v \) is:
\[
A_{vf}' = \frac{A_{vf}'}{1 - A_{tf}'} = \frac{1.5625}{1 - 0.15625} = \frac{1.5625}{0.84375} = 1.84375 \text{ V}
\]

The percent change in the closed-loop gain is:
\[
\Delta A_{vf} = \left( \frac{A_{vf}' - A_{vf}}{A_{vf}} \right) \times 100\% = \left( \frac{1.84375 - (-11.11)}{-11.11} \right) \times 100\% = \left( \frac{12.95375}{-11.11} \right) \times 100\% = -1.165 \times 100\% = -116.5\%
\]

Thus, the percent change in the closed-loop gain is \(\boxed{-116.5\%}\).
