Calculate the change in Gibbs free energy when 2 moles of hydrogen gas react with 1 mole of oxygen gas at a constant temperature of 298 K and a pressure of 1 bar, given the standard Gibbs free energy of formation of water to be -237.1 kJ/mol.<end_of_turn>
