","To find the curl of the vector field \(\mathbf{V}(x, y)\), we first need to express it in terms of its components:

\[
\mathbf{V}(x, y) = \mathbf{i} f(x, y) + \mathbf{j} g(x, y) + \mathbf{k} h(x, y),
\]

where \(f(x, y)\), \(g(x, y)\), and \(h(x, y)\) are scalar functions of \(x\) and \(y\).

The curl of \(\mathbf{V}\), denoted as \(\text{curl} \ \mathbf{V}\), is given by:

\[
\text{curl} \ \mathbf{V} = \frac{\partial}{\partial y} \mathbf{k} \mathbf{V} - \frac{\partial}{\partial x} \mathbf{k} \mathbf{V} = \frac{\partial}{\partial y} \mathbf{k} \mathbf{V} - \frac{\partial}{\partial x} \mathbf{k} \mathbf{V} = \frac{\partial}{\partial y} \mathbf{k} \mathbf{V} - \frac{\partial}{\partial x} \mathbf{k} \mathbf{V}.
\]

Substituting the components of \(\mathbf{V}\):

\[
\text{curl} \ \mathbf{V} = \frac{\partial}{\partial y} \mathbf{k} h(x, y) - \frac{\partial}{\partial x} \mathbf{k} h(x, y).
\]

The curl is a vector, so:

\[
\text{curl} \ \mathbf{V} = \frac{\partial}{\partial y} h(x, y) \mathbf{k} - \frac{\partial}{\partial x} h(x, y) \mathbf{k}.
\]

The curl is a scalar field acting on the \(z\)-axis:

\[
\text{curl} \ \mathbf{V} = \left( \frac{\partial}{\partial y} h(x, y) - \frac{\partial}{\partial x} h(x, y) \right) \mathbf{k}.
\]

Thus, the curl of the vector field \(\mathbf{V}(x, y)\) is:

\[
\boxed{\text{curl} \ \mathbf{V} = \left( \frac{\partial}{\partial y} h(x, y) - \frac{\partial}{\partial x} h(x, y) \right) \mathbf{k}}
\]",fluency,"# Task Description
